Q: How to get the next id in a database table to save an uploaded file in a CodeIgniter application A: <p>Use server time and add some random number to that time to avoid problems when uploading multiple images.     </p>

<pre><code>$imgName = $_FILES["images"]["name"];
$imgTempName = $_FILES["images"]["tmp_name"];
$target_dir = "images/";    
$target_file = $target_dir . basename($imgName);
$imageFileType = strtolower(pathinfo($target_file, PATHINFO_EXTENSION));
//file name uses server time + add random number
$fileName = $target_dir . round(microtime(true) * 10000) . rand() . "." .$imageFileType;

$source_img = $imgTempName;
$destination_img = $fileName;
</code></pre>

Q: Why does my ASP.NET Core seed method only add sample data when the admin user does not exist? A: <p>Ok can i see you program.cs ??</p>
<p>Also make sure u have this at the end of program.cs</p>
<pre><code>using (var scope = app.Services.CreateScope())
{
    var services = scope.ServiceProvider;
    await .Data.SeedData.InitializeAsync(services);
}

And also make sure that in your essentials is like this : 

public class EssentialController : Controller
{
    private readonly ApplicationDbContext _context;

    public EssentialController(ApplicationDbContext context)
    {
        _context = context;
    }

    public async Task&lt;IActionResult&gt; Index(string searchString)
    {
        var items = _context.Items.Where(i =&gt; i.IsActive);

        if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(searchString))
        {
            items = items.Where(i =&gt;
                i.Name.Contains(searchString) ||
                i.Description.Contains(searchString) ||
                i.Category.Contains(searchString));
        }

        return View(await items.ToListAsync());
    }
</code></pre>

Q: How to use Javascript to read local text file and read line by line? A: <p>Files can be processed line by line like this:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>async function * linesFromFile (file)
{
  let textStream = file.stream ().pipeThrough (
    new TextDecoderStream ('utf-8', { fatal: true }));

  let regex = /\r\n?|\n/g;
  let remainder = '';

  for await (let text of textStream)
  {
    text = remainder + text;
    let li = 0;

    regex.lastIndex = remainder.length;
    for (let m; m = regex.exec (text);)
    {
      yield text.slice (li, m.index);
      li = regex.lastIndex;
    }

    remainder = text.slice (li);
  }

  yield remainder;
}
</code></pre>
<p>Usage:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>for await (let line of linesFromFile (file))
  console.log (line);
</code></pre>
